{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ImageDecoding"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Pass data from child views up to their ancestors.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/preferences"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceKey"],"anchor":"Protocols","title":"Protocols"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceValues"],"anchor":"Storage","title":"Storage"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit’s preference system enables "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"bottom-up data flow"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": the reverse of environment values. While the environment passes data down from parent to child, preferences let child views publish values that ancestors can observe and react to."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system mirrors SwiftUI’s preference API and consists of three parts:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceKey","type":"reference","isActive":true}]},{"text":": Protocol that defines a named value type with a default and a reduce strategy","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceValues","type":"reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Type-safe storage that holds all preference values for a scope"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PreferenceStorage","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Stack-based collector that manages preference contexts per render pass","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A built-in example is ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey"},{"text":": a child view sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".navigationTitle(\"Settings\")"},{"text":", and the enclosing navigation container reads that preference to render the title bar.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Defining-a-Preference-Key","level":2,"text":"Defining a Preference Key"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A preference key declares what type of value it carries and how multiple values from sibling children are combined:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct CounterKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: Int = 0","","    static func reduce(value: inout Int, nextValue: () -> Int) {","        value += nextValue()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"defaultValue","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Returned when no child has set this preference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(value:nextValue:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Combines values when multiple children set the same key","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":" implementation simply takes the last value. Override it when you need additive behavior (summing counts), array collection, or other merge strategies.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Setting-a-Preference","level":2,"text":"Setting a Preference"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Child views publish a preference using the ","type":"text"},{"code":".preference(key:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct ItemView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Item\")","            .preference(key: CounterKey.self, value: 1)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Under the hood, this wraps the view in a "},{"code":"PreferenceModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that calls "},{"code":"preferences.setValue(_:forKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" during rendering. The value is reduced into the current scope using the key’s "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function."}]},{"text":"Observing Preferences","anchor":"Observing-Preferences","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ancestor views react to collected preferences using ","type":"text"},{"code":".onPreferenceChange(_:perform:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct ItemList: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","        }","        .onPreferenceChange(CounterKey.self) { totalCount in","            \/\/ totalCount == 3 (three children each set value: 1, additive reduce)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier pushes a new preference context, renders all children (which set their preferences), pops the context, and fires the callback with the accumulated result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-Navigation-Title-Shortcut","type":"heading","text":"The Navigation Title Shortcut"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","type":"reference"},{"text":" as a built-in preference key with a convenience modifier:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct SettingsPage: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            Text(\"App settings go here\")","        }","        .navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationTitleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the default "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (last value wins), so the deepest child’s title takes precedence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"How-Preferences-Flow-per-Frame","type":"heading","text":"How Preferences Flow per Frame"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Preferences are collected fresh every frame. Here’s the lifecycle within a single render pass:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reset"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RenderLoop.render()"},{"text":" calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferences.beginRenderPass()"},{"text":", clearing all callbacks and resetting the stack to a single empty context","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": As the view tree renders top-down, ","type":"text"},{"code":"PreferenceModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" views call ","type":"text"},{"code":"setValue(_:forKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which reduces values into the current stack frame","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OnPreferenceChangeModifier"},{"text":" pushes a new context before rendering its subtree, isolating child preferences","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Collect","type":"text"}]},{"text":": After the subtree finishes, the modifier pops the context (merging into the parent) and fires the callback with the scoped result","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discard"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": At the start of the next frame, everything resets: stale preferences never persist"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This per-frame reset ensures preferences always reflect the current view tree. Removed views stop contributing automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Reduce-Strategies","type":"heading","text":"Reduce Strategies"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function determines how multiple children’s values combine. Common patterns:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strategy"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use Case"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Last value wins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"value = nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (default)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Titles, labels: deepest child wins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Additive"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"value += nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Counting items, summing heights","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Array collection","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathering menu items, breadcrumbs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Array collection example","struct BreadcrumbKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: [String] = []","","    static func reduce(value: inout [String], nextValue: () -> [String]) {","        value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","    }","}"]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"title":"Preferences","role":"collectionGroup"},"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ImageDecoding":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Load static PNG and JPEG images safely on macOS and Linux."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ImageDecoding","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/imagedecoding","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Image Decoding","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ListAndTable":{"kind":"article","title":"List and Table Components","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build scrollable, navigable data collections with keyboard support."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/listandtable","role":"article"},"doc://TUIk